        "original_id": "962d41f7-3cf1-51c1-a5d9-44acce3a852a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ridley Scott, Elmer Clifton, D. W. Griffith, Joseph Henabery, Eric Garcia\n- Films: Alien, Blade Runner, Gladiator, The Martian, The Birth of a Nation, Intolerance, Matchstick Men\n- Roles: film director, producer, actor, collaborator, mentor\n- Works: Matchstick Men novel\n\nFacts:\n- Ridley Scott was born on 30 November 1937 and is an English film director and producer.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in The Birth of a Nation in 1915 as a collaborator of D. W. Griffith.\n- Elmer Clifton appeared in Intolerance in 1916 before giving up acting in 1917 to concentrate on behind-the-camera work.\n- D. W. Griffith and Joseph Henabery were mentors to Elmer Clifton in his behind-the-camera work.\n- Ridley Scott had a commercial breakthrough with the science-fiction horror film Alien in 1979.\n- Ridley Scott's best known works include Blade Runner from 1982, Gladiator from 2000, and The Martian from 2015.\n- Gladiator won the Best Picture Oscar.\n- Matchstick Men is a 2003 British-American black comedy crime film directed by Ridley Scott.\n- Matchstick Men was based on Eric Garcia's 2002 novel of the same name.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
